      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.671,
            0.049,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Finding the Unknown"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.089,
            0.316,
            0.111
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.122,
            0.608,
            0.141
          ],
          "content": "1. Write 5 equations whose solution is x = – 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.146,
            0.667,
            0.246
          ],
          "content": "2. Find the value of each unknown: (a) $2 y = 6 0$ (b) $-8 = 5x - 3$ (c) $- 5 3 w = - 1 5$ (d) $1 3 - \\mathbf { z } = 8$ (e) $k + 8 = 12 - k$ (f) $7 m = m - 3$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.232,
            0.246,
            0.34,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": "3 n = 1 0 + n",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.271,
            0.847,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": "3. I am a 3-digit number. My hundred’s digit is 3 less than my ten’s digit. My ten’s digit is 3 less than my unit’s digit. The sum of all the three digits is 15. Who am I?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.334,
            0.847,
            0.373
          ],
          "content": "4. The weight of a brick is 1 kg more than half its weight. What is the weight of the brick?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.377,
            0.846,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": "5. One quarter of a number increased by 9 gives the same number. What is the number?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.421,
            0.787,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": "6. Given $4 k + 1 = 1 3 ,$ , find the values of: (a) $8 k \\pm 2$ (b) 4k (c) k (d) 4k – 1 (e) – k – 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.498,
            0.698,
            0.522
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "7.3 Mind the Mistake, Mend the Mistake"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.531,
            0.847,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": "? The following are some equations along with the steps used to solve them to find the value of the letter−number. Go through each solution and decide whether the steps are correct. If there is a mistake, describe the mistake, correct it and solve the equation."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.628,
            0.242,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": "1"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.243,
            0.647,
            0.355,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{cases}4x + 6 = 10 \\\\4x = 10 + 6 \\\\4x = 16 \\\\x = 4\\end{cases}",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.424,
            0.628,
            0.443,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": "2"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.443,
            0.646,
            0.541,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{cases}7 - 8z = 5 \\\\8z = 7 - 5 \\\\8z = 2 \\\\z = 4\\end{cases}",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.626,
            0.628,
            0.645,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": "3"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.649,
            0.647,
            0.767,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{cases}2v - 4 = 6 \\\\v - 4 = 6 - 2 \\\\v - 4 = 4 \\\\v = 8\\end{cases}",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.224,
            0.746,
            0.243,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": "4"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.242,
            0.764,
            0.401,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{cases}5z + 2 = 3z - 4 \\\\5z + 3z = -4 + 2 \\\\8z = -2 \\\\z = -\\dfrac{2}{8}\\end{cases}",
          "image_source": "images/page_17_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.426,
            0.746,
            0.444,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": "5"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
